------------------------------------------------------------------------
Explicit CRT reading of the user's instances:
  n=14: residue 7 -> (7 mod 2, 7 mod 7) = (7%2=1, 7%7=0)  = 2-torsion gen, 0 in 7-base
  n=15: residue 5 -> (5 mod 3, 5 mod 5) = (2, 0)  = 3-torsion, 0 in 5-base
  n=15: residue 10 -> (10 mod 3, 10 mod 5) = (1, 0)  = 3-torsion, 0 in 5-base

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Union of prime-torsion subgroups (single-prime-surviving leaks) & hard core:
  n=14: U(T_p\0)=[2, 4, 6, 7, 8, 10, 12]; hard core (0 in all primes, mod n) = [0] (incl 0)
  n=15: U(T_p\0)=[3, 5, 6, 9, 10, 12]; hard core (0 in all primes, mod n) = [0] (incl 0)
  n=30: U(T_p\0)=[6, 10, 12, 15, 18, 20, 24]; hard core (0 in all primes, mod n) = [0] (incl 0)
  n=12: U(T_p\0)=[4, 6, 8]; hard core (0 in all primes, mod n) = [0, 6] (incl 0)

GEOMETRIC localization (torsion sits at order-p rotations, ||.||>=1/p) holds for ALL n: True
SQUAREFREE clean plug (socle survives mod p, plugged by t=1/p):  True
=> squarefree primes: leak plugged by the prime clock (margin 1/p);
   prime-power factors: socle torsion is itself ≡0 mod p, needs the deeper p-adic clock
   -- this is the prime-power hardness (cf. n=14: 2n-1=27=3^3, no coprime plug).
